<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">North German Confederation</h1><p class="st-meta">1867 CE – 1871 CE · capital Berlin</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Prussian-led federal state formed after the defeat of Austria in 1866, the direct forerunner of the German Empire.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia's</a> victory in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-prussian-war">Austro-Prussian War</a> of 1866 dissolved the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/german-confederation">German Confederation</a>. Prussia annexed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanover">Hanover</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/electorate-of-hesse">Hesse-Kassel</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-nassau">Nassau</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a> and joined the remaining states north of the Main in a new federation. Its constitution, drafted largely by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-von-bismarck">Otto von Bismarck</a>, came into force on 1 July 1867.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> held the federal presidency and commanded the armies, and Bismarck was federal chancellor. A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundesrat-german-empire">Federal Council</a> represented the governments, and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reichstag">Reichstag</a> was elected by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/universal-suffrage">universal male suffrage</a>. The confederation unified weights and measures, trade law and criminal law, and the south German states were tied to it by military alliances and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/customs-union">customs union</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-prussian-war">Franco-Prussian War</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, Württemberg, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden">Baden</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a> joined in 1870. The confederation was renamed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/german-empire">German Empire</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelm-i">William I</a> was proclaimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-emperor">German Emperor</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a> on 18 January 1871.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/north-german-confederation.jpg" alt="North German Confederation" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Original: Adolf Soetbeer, Otto von Bismarck Vector: B1mbo, Madden · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Germany_(1867%E2%80%931918).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1867 CE – 1871 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Berlin</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>William I, Otto von Bismarck</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism, Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a>, <a href="/countries/poland">Poland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Norddeutscher Bund</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1869&amp;focus=north-german-confederation" aria-label="North German Confederation on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4980 366 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where North German Confederation lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5300 622L5300 622M5300 622L5300 622M5300 622L5312 664M5300 622L5276 641M5300 622L5199 691"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5300 622h0M5300 622h0M5312 664h0M5276 641h0M5199 691h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5300 622h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5300 622h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Berlin. <a href="/atlas?year=1869&amp;focus=north-german-confederation">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
